No third-party source code is included. The scripts import TokenGate
(https://github.com/token-gate-llms/TokenGate, Apache-2.0), transformers and
compressed-tensors (Apache-2.0), PyTorch (BSD-3-Clause), vLLM
(https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm) and pth-flash-attn
(https://github.com/noon-at-cgn/pth-flash-attn) (Apache-2.0).

Benchmarks load SCBench (https://huggingface.co/datasets/microsoft/SCBench, MIT)
and the TokenGate NIAH samples at run time; neither dataset is redistributed.
The needle-in-a-haystack method follows Greg Kamradt's NIAH
(https://github.com/gkamradt/LLMTest_NeedleInAHaystack, MIT, Copyright (c) 2023
Greg Kamradt). Essay text quoted in recorded results has been redacted (the
essays are copyrighted by their author).

Models used: Qwen3.5-2B, Qwen3.5-9B and Qwen3.8-27B (Apache-2.0, Alibaba Cloud /
Qwen team), and liana313/tokengate-niah-qwen3.5-2b (Apache-2.0).
